Z||000000||firstfiero||03-18-2001||03:06 PM||||      I've only had my fiero on the highway a couple of times and it always seemed real loose. I thought maybe it was because of no weight on the front and that big rear spoiler in the back creating to much down force. Today I made sure my tires had proper preasure the whole way around...I have some slow leaks....and then took her out on the highway. She was perfect! I only have the se speedo...but I had that buried befor I even got off the exit ramp. I had to be going 100+ with a slightly windy day and she was like a rock. did the same thing on my way back and got the same results. Any of you guys have that loosey feeling when driving on the highway? would sway bars help tighten up my ride? later||||reg||7
Z||000001||fropuff||03-18-2001||06:47 PM||||Today I got up to 113 in the GT.  Sssh!  Don't tell My7Fieros!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  It was a little windy, but it did pretty good.  Mine isn't really loose, but it was pretty windy.  Otherwise, it's very tight and responsive.  Gotta watch out for the heat though!  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||03-18-2001||07:58 PM||||that rear downforce your feeling is imaginary. Unless its sticking straight up in the air like a late model stock car it wont do anything below 150MPH except keep the dust off the tail lites. There just there to look cool.||||reg||1
